{
  "matches": [
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n1"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "To initiate the process for the election of a rector, it is necessary to begin with the rector's final year in their current position."
      ],
      "justification": "The initiator and first action jointly capture the process start and the requirement to begin with the rector's final year."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n2"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Following this, the acceptance of proposals for candidates for the rector position should be launched."
      ],
      "justification": "Direct paraphrase of launching proposal acceptance."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n3"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Once this is done, the rector can nominate themselves as a candidate for the position."
      ],
      "justification": "Accurately captures the self-nomination step."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n4"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "After the nominations have been made, the acceptance of proposals should be stopped."
      ],
      "justification": "Matches the stopping of proposal acceptance."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b1->n6",
        "action:n6"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If a candidate meets the required criteria, they should be included in the list of candidates."
      ],
      "justification": "The XOR branch and boolean guard correctly model the positive criterion check, leading to inclusion in the list."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b1->n7",
        "action:n7"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "However, if a candidate does not meet the criteria, they should be informed of the refusal and the process will come to an end."
      ],
      "justification": "Models the negative criterion path, informing of refusal, and terminating the process via the end node."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n8"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Once the list of candidates has been formed, it should be made public."
      ],
      "justification": "Direct match for publishing the candidate list."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n9"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Simultaneously, the candidates should promote their ideas to the public and organize a public meeting of the Academic Senate."
      ],
      "justification": "Captures the simultaneous campaign and meeting organization step."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n11"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "The public meeting should then commence, ensuring that all members are able to vote for a new rector."
      ],
      "justification": "Matches the commencement of the public meeting for voting."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n12"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "Following the meeting, an election should be conducted and the votes should be counted."
      ],
      "justification": "Direct match for conducting the election and counting votes."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b_elec->n13",
        "action:n13"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "If the voting fails, another election should be conducted."
      ],
      "justification": "Models the failure condition looping back to conduct another election. Boolean guard preserves the decision logic."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "guard:b_elec->n14",
        "action:n14"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "On the other hand, if the voting is successful, the result of the election should be announced."
      ],
      "justification": "Models the success condition leading to result announcement."
    },
    {
      "refs": [
        "action:n15",
        "action:n16",
        "action:n17"
      ],
      "verbatim_texts": [
        "After announcing the result, the public meeting should be concluded and the candidate should be informed of the election results, marking the end of the process."
      ],
      "justification": "The source sentence is split into three sequential actions (conclude meeting, inform candidate, end process) plus the structural end node. Splitting a compound step is behaviour-preserving and thus a match."
    }
  ],
